7. PERSONA - Skills say how, a persona says who
======================================================
* "Skills say how. A persona says who."
- "A persona is a role description, like one for a new
  hire: your role, your standards, what you never do."
- Point at Hard limits: "This matters most. No cloud
  credentials, never applies infrastructure. A person
  approves."
- "My junior and senior DevOps kits share the exact same
  skills. The junior runs on a cheaper model and stops at
  IAM, networking and state, then flags its PR for senior
  review. Same procedures, different judgment."
> "So how do I put a persona and skills together?
   That's a kit."

